  "notes": "{拭|ふ}く is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) for wiping surfaces clean or dry.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{拭|ふ}いている indicates wiping is in progress.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [surface]を{拭|ふ}く — to wipe [surface]\n- [moisture/dirt]を{拭|ふ}く — to wipe away [moisture/dirt]\n- [cloth]で{拭|ふ}く — to wipe with [cloth]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {汗|あせ}を{拭|ふ}く (wipe sweat)\n- {涙|なみだ}を{拭|ふ}く (wipe tears)\n- {床|ゆか}を{拭|ふ}く (wipe/mop the floor)\n- {拭|ふ}き{掃除|そうじ} (wiping/mopping)\n\nDO NOT CONFUSE:\n- {拭|ふ}く (to wipe) — different from:\n- {吹|ふ}く (to blow)\n- {噴|ふ}く (to spout)\n\nAll three can be read ふく but have different meanings.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {雑巾|ぞうきん} (cleaning rag)\n- {拭|ふ}き{取|と}る (to wipe off)",
